{"title":"Career Roadmap — Quality Control Manager","role":"Quality Control Manager","summary":"A Quality Control Manager in the sugar, oil, paint or rubber industries is responsible for ensuring that raw materials, manufacturing processes and finished products consistently meet defined quality, safety, performance and regulatory specifications.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Sugar / Oil / Paint / Rubber Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Quality Control Manager in the sugar, oil, paint or rubber industries is responsible for ensuring that raw materials, manufacturing processes and finished products consistently meet defined quality, safety, performance and regulatory specifications."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Industrial chemistry"},{"text":"Process engineering"},{"text":"Laboratory testing"},{"text":"Quality systems"},{"text":"Statistical quality control"},{"text":"Root-cause analysis"},{"text":"Process improvement"},{"text":"Regulatory compliance"},{"text":"Team and laboratory management"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The graduate should ideally build cross-industry QC fundamentals while developing deeper expertise in one sector such as sugar processing, edible/non-edible oils, paints/coatings or rubber products."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Tech/B.E."},{"text":"Process technology, chemistry, laboratory testing and QC"}],[{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"QC Trainee / Quality Engineer"},{"text":"Testing, inspection, documentation and SPC"}],[{"text":"2033–2037"},{"text":"QC Engineer / Executive"},{"text":"Process and product quality management"}],[{"text":"2037–2041"},{"text":"Senior QC Engineer / Assistant Manager"},{"text":"Laboratory, process quality and improvement"}],[{"text":"2041–2046"},{"text":"Quality Control Manager"},{"text":"Quality strategy, teams, audits and compliance"}]]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"“Manager” is generally an experience-level position rather than a direct graduate entry role. A fresh graduate normally enters through QC/QA trainee, quality engineer, laboratory or process-quality positions."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During the Degree","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Scientific & Engineering Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong fundamentals in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Engineering chemistry"},{"text":"Mathematics"},{"text":"Physics"},{"text":"Engineering mechanics"},{"text":"Basic electrical/electronics"},{"text":"Computer applications"},{"text":"Engineering drawing"},{"text":"Laboratory safety"},{"text":"Technical communication"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop basic understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Measurement systems"},{"text":"Units and conversions"},{"text":"Chemical concentration"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Experimental error"},{"text":"Accuracy vs precision"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Process & Quality Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Industrial chemistry"},{"text":"Thermodynamics"},{"text":"Fluid mechanics"},{"text":"Heat transfer"},{"text":"Mass transfer"},{"text":"Chemical/process engineering"},{"text":"Material science"},{"text":"Industrial instrumentation"},{"text":"Process control"},{"text":"Manufacturing processes"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Begin learning:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Quality control"},{"text":"Quality assurance"},{"text":"Inspection"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Standard operating procedures"},{"text":"Laboratory documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Industry-Specific Quality"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose at least one primary domain."},{"type":"h","text":"Sugar Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"tex